# DISHA 6.6 Agent Rules

DISHA is an evidence-first governance intelligence system. Follow these rules when changing the repository.

## Scope

- Treat `web/` as the active production product.
- Keep `disha/`, `skills/`, and `legacy/` behind explicit governed adapters unless the task specifically targets research or maintenance there.
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `ARCHITECTURE.md` before changing core behavior.

## Non-negotiable controls

- Validate all external input with typed schemas.
- Authenticate and authorize every sensitive request.
- Enforce resource ownership for reads, writes, shares, missions, and evidence.
- Never trust client-supplied paths, roles, model names, URLs, or user IDs.
- Never commit secrets or log raw credentials and unnecessary PII.
- Use the persistent PostgreSQL evidence/audit stores in production; in-memory stores are test or explicitly local-development fallbacks only.
- Model output is advisory, provenance-bound, policy-gated, and never a source of fact.
- Deny offensive cyber actions and preserve safe, read-only fallbacks.

## Change standard

Every production change should satisfy:

`contract -> policy -> evidence -> test`

Run the web type check, tests, and build before handoff. Update the relevant documentation when behavior or architecture changes.
